cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this work, please cite it as below."
title: "Friction keeps the conservation laws of training alive: exact drift identities for heavy ball and Nesterov momentum"
authors:
  - family-names: Gaur
    given-names: Pragyaan
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0009-0009-4037-2478"
repository-code: "https://github.com/pragyaangaur/Viscous-Conservation-Laws"
license: MIT
version: "1.0.0"
date-released: "2026-10-21"
keywords:
  - conservation laws
  - momentum
  - heavy ball
  - Nesterov acceleration
  - implicit bias
  - Lean 4
abstract: >-
  Exact identities and uniform-in-time bounds for how heavy ball and Nesterov momentum
  break the quadratic conservation laws that symmetries give a network, with a proof that
  Nesterov's schedule keeps a step-size independent drift for positive semidefinite
  generators. The identities and finite-time bounds are formalised in Lean 4 with Mathlib.
